<TITLE>CAN Communication Network</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>By dividing the CAN communication main line into 2 systems (V bus system/MS bus system) via the meter ECU, the communication load within the CAN communication bus due to the increased number of connected computers has been reduced.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The CAN communication system is configured as a bus type network in which multiple computers are connected to 2 common communication lines; the CAN communication lines used as the main lines (common communication lines) are V bus No.1 (communication speed 500kbs) from the meter ECU to the engine control ECU, V bus No.2 (communication speed 500kbs) from the CAN gateway computer to junction connector No.4, and the MS bus (communication speed 250kbs) from the meter ECU to the Main Body ECU.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Terminating resistors (120 Ω) are provided on the bus main line. This allows the differential voltage to be determined from the loop-connected network.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
